# Warpline: ignore the heavy/regenerable store (WARP snapshots + oracle log), but
# TRACK this project's native meaning-history — the fabric ledger + the selvage
# tip — so it pushes with git (coexistence). State snapshots are reconstructable
# by re-absorbing each strand's provenance.gitCommit, so they stay ignored.
.warpline/*
!.warpline/fabric.jsonl
!.warpline/fabric-legacy.json
!.warpline/refs/
.warpline/refs/*
!.warpline/refs/selvage
# (legacy Loom runtime dir, kept ignored for back-compat)
.loom/
